IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc26-interpretation`

-- ccc26-discharge.l4 -- sections 729.2 and 730 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: the order prohibiting contact, and absolute and
-- conditional discharges (lines 15468-15495 of the text). Layer 1 of part ccc26. The text is a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the
-- Justice Laws Website consolidation; it is not the official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.

§ `Section 729.2 -- Order prohibiting contact`

-- (1): "the court ... may make an order prohibiting the offender from having any contact". The gate is "When an offender is convicted, or is discharged
-- under section 730 on the conditions prescribed in a probation order, of an offence that is ..." (a "When" gate: JUST FALSE where it fails; listed in the
-- name-test sweep, group (i)); the three kinds of offence are a scope that is not closed with "only" (NOTHING for another kind).
-- src:15468 | Order Prohibiting Contact
-- src:15469 | Order prohibiting contact
-- src:15470 | 729.2 (1) When an offender is convicted, or is discharged under section 730 on the conditions prescribed in a probation order, of an offence that is of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose, an offence related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons or an offence committed against their intimate partner, the court that imposes a sentence on the offender or directs the discharge may make an order prohibiting the offender from having any contact — including by communicating by any means — with any victim, witness or other person identified in the order except in accordance with any conditions specified in the order that the court considers necessary.
@ref s 729.2(1) (src:15468-15470)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is discharged under section 730 on the conditions prescribed in a probation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is the court that imposes a sentence on the offender or directs the discharge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 intimate partner: the offence was committed against the offender's intimate partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 729.2(1) the court may make an order prohibiting the offender from having any contact` MEANS   -- gate: when (the offender is convicted, or discharged under section 730 on the conditions prescribed in a probation order)
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the offender is convicted`) AND (NOT `the offender is discharged under section 730 on the conditions prescribed in a probation order`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When an offender is convicted, or is discharged under section 730 on the conditions prescribed in a probation order, of an offence"
        IF NOT `the court is the court that imposes a sentence on the offender or directs the discharge` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court that imposes a sentence on the offender or directs the discharge may make an order"
        IF `the offence is of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose` OR `the offence is related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2 intimate partner: the offence was committed against the offender's intimate partner` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2 intimate partner: the offence was committed against the offender's intimate partner` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is the offender's intimate partner is for section 2
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence that is of a sexual nature or committed for a sexual purpose, an offence related to criminal harassment or trafficking in persons or an offence committed against their intimate partner"

-- (2): "The prohibition may be for life or for any shorter duration that the court considers desirable."
-- src:15471 | Duration of prohibition
-- src:15472 | (2) The prohibition may be for life or for any shorter duration that the court considers desirable.
@ref s 729.2(2) (src:15471-15472)
GIVEN `the prohibition is for life` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prohibition is for a shorter duration that the court considers desirable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 729.2(2) the prohibition may be for the duration` MEANS   -- gate: none (the limit is on the duration the grant reaches)
    IF `the prohibition is for life` OR `the prohibition is for a shorter duration that the court considers desirable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The prohibition may be for life or for any shorter duration that the court considers desirable"

-- (3): variation, "on application of the person identified in the order or the prosecutor" and "after hearing the parties", "if, in its opinion, the variation is desirable".
-- src:15473 | Variation of order
-- src:15474 | (3) A court of competent jurisdiction may, on application of the person identified in the order or the prosecutor, require the offender to appear before it at any time and, after hearing the parties, the court may vary the order if, in its opinion, the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances after the conditions were prescribed.
@ref s 729.2(3) (src:15473-15474)
GIVEN `the court is a court of competent jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person identified in the order or the prosecutor applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 729.2(3) the court may require the offender to appear before it` MEANS   -- gate: on (application of the person identified in the order or the prosecutor)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is a court of competent jurisdiction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court of competent jurisdiction may"
        IF NOT `the person identified in the order or the prosecutor applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the person identified in the order or the prosecutor"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 729.2(3) (src:15473-15474)
GIVEN `the court is a court of competent jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has heard the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the court's opinion the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances after the conditions were prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 729.2(3) the court may vary the order` MEANS   -- gate: after (hearing the parties), if (the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is a court of competent jurisdiction` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A court of competent jurisdiction may"
        IF NOT `the court has heard the parties` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after hearing the parties, the court may vary the order"
        IF NOT `in the court's opinion the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances after the conditions were prescribed` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if, in its opinion, the variation is desirable because of changed circumstances after the conditions were prescribed"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (4): which court the application is made to.
-- src:15475 | Court of competent jurisdiction
-- src:15476 | (4) The application shall be made to
-- src:15477 | (a) if an order was made under subsection (1), the court that made the order or, if that court is for any reason unable to act, another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province; or
-- src:15478 | (b) if an order was made under subsection 203.73(1) of the National Defence Act and the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 203.73(4) of that Act, a superior court of criminal jurisdiction.
@ref s 729.2(4) (src:15475-15478)
DECLARE `s 729.2(4) court the application is made to` IS ONE OF
    `s 729.2(4)(a) the court that made the order`
    `s 729.2(4)(a) another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province`
    `s 729.2(4)(b) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`

@ref s 729.2(4) (src:15475-15478)
GIVEN `an order was made under subsection 729.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court that made the order is for any reason unable to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order was made under subsection 203.73(1) of the National Defence Act and the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 203.73(4) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 729.2(4) court the application is made to`
`s 729.2(4) the court the application must be made to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an order was made under subsection 729.2(1)` AND (NOT `the court that made the order is for any reason unable to act`) THEN JUST `s 729.2(4)(a) the court that made the order`
        IF `an order was made under subsection 729.2(1)` THEN JUST `s 729.2(4)(a) another court of equivalent jurisdiction in the same province`
        IF `an order was made under subsection 203.73(1) of the National Defence Act and the Chief Military Judge does not have jurisdiction to receive the application under subsection 203.73(4) of that Act` THEN JUST `s 729.2(4)(b) a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection names the court for an order under subsection (1) and for the National Defence Act case, and no other

-- (5): the offence of failing to comply, and its two penalties (the second states none: section 787, outside this part's text, supplies the summary penalty).
-- src:15479 | Failure to comply with order
-- src:15480 | (5) Every person who fails, without lawful excuse, to comply with an order made under subsection (1) is
-- src:15481 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years; or
-- src:15482 | (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 729.2(5) (src:15479-15482)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with an order made under subsection 729.2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 729.2(5) the person is guilty of the offence of failing to comply with the order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person fails to comply with an order made under subsection 729.2(1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who fails, without lawful excuse, to comply with an order made under subsection (1) is"
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 729.2(5)(a) (src:15479-15481)
`s 729.2(5)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 729.2(5)(b) (src:15482)
`s 729.2(5)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref s 729.2(5) (src:15479-15482)
`s 729.2(5) the class of offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Section 730 -- Conditional and absolute discharge`

-- Whether a minimum punishment is prescribed, and whether the offence is punishable by imprisonment for fourteen years or for life, are read off the
-- offence section's punishment (the seam input of PLAN.md); each answers NOTHING when the offence section is silent.
-- src:15484 | Absolute and Conditional Discharges
-- src:15485 | Conditional and absolute discharge
-- src:15486 | 730 (1) Where an accused, other than an organization, pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence, other than an offence for which a minimum punishment is prescribed by law or an offence punishable by imprisonment for fourteen years or for life, the court before which the accused appears may, if it considers it to be in the best interests of the accused and not contrary to the public interest, instead of convicting the accused, by order direct that the accused be discharged absolutely or on the conditions prescribed in a probation order made under subsection 731(2).
@ref s 730(1) (src:15484-15486)
GIVEN `the punishment the offence charged is liable to (from the offence section itself)` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 730(1) the offence has a minimum punishment prescribed by law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the punishment the offence charged is liable to (from the offence section itself)`'s `minimum imprisonment` EQUALS `no imprisonment is stated`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT (`the punishment the offence charged is liable to (from the offence section itself)`'s `minimum fine` EQUALS `no fine is stated`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the offence section states no minimum, and another enactment may prescribe one

@ref s 730(1) (src:15484-15486)
GIVEN `the punishment the offence charged is liable to (from the offence section itself)` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 730(1) the offence is punishable by imprisonment for fourteen years or for life` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the punishment the offence charged is liable to (from the offence section itself)`'s `maximum imprisonment`
    WHEN `imprisonment for life` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `no imprisonment is stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the offence section states no maximum imprisonment
    WHEN `imprisonment for a term of` term THEN `s 716 the first period is at most the second period` `fourteen years` term

@ref s 730(1) (src:15484-15486)
GIVEN `the accused is an organization` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a minimum punishment is prescribed by law for the offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the offence is punishable by imprisonment for fourteen years or for life` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it to be in the best interests of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers it not contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 730(1) the court may direct that the accused be discharged instead of convicting the accused` MEANS   -- gate: where (an accused, other than an organization, pleads guilty or is found guilty of an offence, other than ...), if (the court considers it in the best interests of the accused and not contrary to the public interest)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused, other than an organization, pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence"
        IF `the accused is an organization` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an accused, other than an organization, pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence"
        IF `a minimum punishment is prescribed by law for the offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than an offence for which a minimum punishment is prescribed by law"
        IF `the offence is punishable by imprisonment for fourteen years or for life` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "or an offence punishable by imprisonment for fourteen years or for life"
        IF (`a minimum punishment is prescribed by law for the offence` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the offence is punishable by imprisonment for fourteen years or for life` EQUALS NOTHING) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence has a minimum punishment, or carries fourteen years or life, is for the offence section
        IF (NOT `the court considers it to be in the best interests of the accused`) OR (NOT `the court considers it not contrary to the public interest`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it considers it to be in the best interests of the accused and not contrary to the public interest"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2): the appearance notice, summons, undertaking or release order continues in force until a disposition under (1), unless the court orders custody.
-- src:15487 | Period for which appearance notice, etc., continues in force
-- src:15488 | (2) Subject to Part XVI, if an accused who has not been taken into custody or who has been released from custody under any provision of that Part pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence but is not convicted, the appearance notice, summons, undertaking or release order issued to, given or entered into by the accused continues in force, subject to its terms, until a disposition in respect of the accused is made under subsection (1) unless, at the time the accused pleads guilty or is found guilty, the court, judge or justice orders that the accused be taken into custody pending such a disposition.
@ref s 730(2) (src:15487-15488)
GIVEN `the accused has not been taken into custody or has been released from custody under a provision of Part XVI` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence but is not convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a disposition in respect of the accused has been made under subsection 730(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the accused pleads guilty or is found guilty the court, judge or justice orders that the accused be taken into custody pending the disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 730(2) the appearance notice, summons, undertaking or release order continues in force` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the accused has not been taken into custody or has been released from custody under a provision of Part XVI`) OR (NOT `the accused pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence but is not convicted`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if an accused who has not been taken into custody or who has been released from custody under any provision of that Part pleads guilty to or is found guilty of an offence but is not convicted"
        IF `a disposition in respect of the accused has been made under subsection 730(1)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until a disposition in respect of the accused is made under subsection (1)"
        IF `at the time the accused pleads guilty or is found guilty the court, judge or justice orders that the accused be taken into custody pending the disposition` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless, at the time the accused pleads guilty or is found guilty, the court, judge or justice orders that the accused be taken into custody pending such a disposition"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (3): the effect of a discharge.
-- src:15489 | Effect of discharge
-- src:15490 | (3) Where a court directs under subsection (1) that an offender be discharged of an offence, the offender shall be deemed not to have been convicted of the offence except that
@ref s 730(3) (src:15489-15490)
GIVEN `a court directs under subsection 730(1) that the offender be discharged of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 730(3) the offender is deemed not to have been convicted of the offence` MEANS
    IF `a court directs under subsection 730(1) that the offender be discharged of the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a court directs under subsection (1) that an offender be discharged of an offence, the offender shall be deemed not to have been convicted of the offence"

-- src:15491 | (a) the offender may appeal from the determination of guilt as if it were a conviction in respect of the offence;
@ref s 730(3)(a) (src:15491)
GIVEN `a court directs under subsection 730(1) that the offender be discharged of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 730(3)(a) the offender may appeal from the determination of guilt as if it were a conviction` MEANS   -- gate: where (a court directs under subsection (1) that an offender be discharged)
    IF `a court directs under subsection 730(1) that the offender be discharged of the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court directs under subsection (1) that an offender be discharged of an offence, the offender shall be deemed not to have been convicted of the offence except that"

-- src:15492 | (b) the Attorney General and, in the case of summary conviction proceedings, the informant or the informant’s agent may appeal from the decision of the court not to convict the offender of the offence as if that decision were a judgment or verdict of acquittal of the offence or a dismissal of the information against the offender; and
@ref s 730(3)(b) (src:15492)
GIVEN `a court directs under subsection 730(1) that the offender be discharged of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 Attorney General: the person is the Attorney General` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are summary conviction proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the informant or the informant's agent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 730(3)(b) the person may appeal from the decision not to convict the offender as if it were an acquittal or a dismissal of the information` MEANS   -- gate: where (a court directs under subsection (1) that an offender be discharged)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a court directs under subsection 730(1) that the offender be discharged of the offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court directs under subsection (1) that an offender be discharged of an offence, the offender shall be deemed not to have been convicted of the offence except that"
        IF `s 2 Attorney General: the person is the Attorney General` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the proceedings are summary conviction proceedings` AND `the person is the informant or the informant's agent` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2 Attorney General: the person is the Attorney General` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who is the Attorney General for this proceeding is for section 2
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Attorney General and, in the case of summary conviction proceedings, the informant or the informant's agent may appeal"

-- src:15493 | (c) the offender may plead autrefois convict in respect of any subsequent charge relating to the offence.
@ref s 730(3)(c) (src:15493)
GIVEN `a court directs under subsection 730(1) that the offender be discharged of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subsequent charge relates to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 730(3)(c) the offender may plead autrefois convict in respect of any subsequent charge relating to the offence` MEANS   -- gate: where (a court directs under subsection (1) that an offender be discharged)
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a court directs under subsection 730(1) that the offender be discharged of the offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a court directs under subsection (1) that an offender be discharged of an offence, the offender shall be deemed not to have been convicted of the offence except that"
        IF NOT `the subsequent charge relates to the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of any subsequent charge relating to the offence"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (4): revocation of the discharge by the court that made the probation order.
-- src:15494 | Where person bound by probation order convicted of offence
-- src:15495 | (4) Where an offender who is bound by the conditions of a probation order made at a time when the offender was directed to be discharged under this section is convicted of an offence, including an offence under section 733.1, the court that made the probation order may, in addition to or in lieu of exercising its authority under subsection 732.2(5), at any time when it may take action under that subsection, revoke the discharge, convict the offender of the offence to which the discharge relates and impose any sentence that could have been imposed if the offender had been convicted at the time of discharge, and no appeal lies from a conviction under this subsection where an appeal was taken from the order directing that the offender be discharged.
@ref s 730(4) (src:15494-15495)
GIVEN `the offender is bound by the conditions of a probation order made at a time when the offender was directed to be discharged under section 730` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is convicted of an offence, including an offence under section 733.1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is the court that made the probation order and acts at a time when it may take action under subsection 732.2(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 730(4) the court may revoke the discharge, convict the offender and impose any sentence that could have been imposed at the time of discharge` MEANS   -- gate: where (the offender is bound by the conditions of a probation order made on a discharge, and is convicted of an offence)
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the offender is bound by the conditions of a probation order made at a time when the offender was directed to be discharged under section 730`) OR (NOT `the offender is convicted of an offence, including an offence under section 733.1`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offender who is bound by the conditions of a probation order made at a time when the offender was directed to be discharged under this section is convicted of an offence, including an offence under section 733.1, the court that made the probation order may"
        IF NOT `the court is the court that made the probation order and acts at a time when it may take action under subsection 732.2(5)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court that made the probation order may, in addition to or in lieu of exercising its authority under subsection 732.2(5), at any time when it may take action under that subsection"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 730(4) (src:15494-15495)
GIVEN `the conviction is made under subsection 730(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an appeal was taken from the order directing that the offender be discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 730(4) an appeal from the conviction is barred` MEANS
    IF `the conviction is made under subsection 730(4)` AND `an appeal was taken from the order directing that the offender be discharged`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no appeal lies from a conviction under this subsection where an appeal was taken from the order directing that the offender be discharged"
